    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31616" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκᾰτηβόλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκατᾱ</span></b>  - (q.v.), epith. of
		Apollo, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hes.
		</span></i>: as Subst., <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			15.231
		</span></i> ; also of Artemis, <i><span class="en">
			<u>h.Hom.</u>
			9.6
		</span></i>. (Expld. by the ancients as, =
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>far-darting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, etc. (or, <i>shooting a hundred</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βέλη,</span> Id.) ; but perh. originally,
				<i>hitting the mark at will,</i> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάεργος.</span>)</div>
